<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gerald FitzGerald, 3rd Earl of Desmond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1338–<a href="/years/1398">1398</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Gearóid Iarla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gerald FitzGerald, 3rd Earl of Desmond, known in Irish as Gearóid Iarla, was a Hiberno-Norman lord who served as Justiciar of Ireland from 1367. He is best known as a poet in the Irish language, whose courtly love poems are among the earliest of their kind in Irish. Legend says he did not die but sleeps beneath Lough Gur in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-limerick">County Limerick</a>.</p></div>
